  "interpretation": [
    "The nine-state workload measures first insertion into a fresh real SQLite store; full-engine write timing measures nine same-value updates after explicit migration in the new mode. The baseline has no state migration and preserves plain rows. These are distinct write cases, not browser capture throughput.",
    "Full-engine migration temporarily adds WAL while the main file retains free pages. Only explicit compact reclaims file bytes. The report includes initial, post-migration, active and closed DB/WAL/SHM separately.",
    "Memory figures are process measurements from isolated workers. Peak RSS includes engine-wide decoding/hash verification and migration, and is not attributable solely to state codec buffers. No persistent state cache was introduced. Post-GC heap and ArrayBuffer figures are included; external Buffer accounting and allocator retention vary, so negative before/after deltas are not a memory-saving claim.",
    "The full-engine snapshot contains all entity kinds and all 14 observations. Their decoded hashes, 1325 referenced objects and 80 packs remain identical across baseline/new/migration/restart runs. External evidence files are not copied or benchmarked.",
    "Neither workload includes real page capture, provider/model network latency, browser recovery or an end-to-end OKX run. Cold read means first list after Store reopen, with OS cache not flushed. Performance conclusions apply to this nine-state snapshot on this machine only."
  ]
